  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;be two <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;real matrices such that&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced></math> is invertible matrix. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>5</mn></msup></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;then the value of the determinant of the matrix <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math> is equal to :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>;</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mi>C</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Subtracting equation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math>&nbsp;from&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math>, we get&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mfenced><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mfenced><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>O</mi></math></p><p>Post multiplying inverse of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>:</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>O</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p>"
  }
